  "claim": "For any admitted finite tokenomics trace, if each reward/rebate/bounty/buyback step is funded by newly verified value plus treasury or resource drawdown, then cumulative spend over the trace is bounded by cumulative verified value gained plus initial treasury. If a trace creates no verified value and consumes no treasury/resource budget, funded nondecreasing rewards cannot increase; a positive payout over such a loop proves the stepwise funding predicate was violated. If cumulative spend exceeds the verified-value-plus-budget bound, the stepwise funding predicate is impossible. A reward controller guard packages nonnegative reward spend, nonnegative verified value gain, and the fail-closed aggregate spend bound.",
  "result": "proved",
